# Migrate to Supabase & Website Optimization

This plan outlines the steps we will take to migrate the project's database to Supabase PostgreSQL, integrate Supabase Authentication (including Google OAuth), and optimize the application's performance and SEO.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> This requires you to create a **Supabase Project** in your Supabase dashboard. Once created, you will need to retrieve the database connection string and API keys to put in your [.env](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/.env) file before these changes will fully work. You will also need to re-run your database creation (Prisma migrations) against the new cloud database, since your old data is currently stored in a local SQLite file ([dev.db](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/dev.db)), which we will be removing.

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Database & Dependencies Migration

We will swap out SQLite for Supabase's hosted PostgreSQL.
- **[MODIFY]** [package.json](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/package.json): Remove `better-sqlite3`, `@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3`. Add `@supabase/supabase-js` and `@supabase/ssr`.
- **[MODIFY]** [prisma/schema.prisma](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/prisma/schema.prisma): Change the `provider` from `sqlite` to `postgresql`. Add support for a connection pooler `url` and a `directUrl`.
- **[MODIFY]** [.env.example](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/.env.example): Add placeholders for `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL` and `DIRECT_URL`.
- **[DELETE]** [dev.db](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/dev.db) and any SQLite config files to prevent conflicts.

### Phase 2: Supabase SSR Authentication

Since we're using Supabase, it handles user sign-in and passwords securely for us.
- **[NEW]** `src/lib/server/supabase.js`: Helper functions to create server-side Supabase clients.
- **[MODIFY]** [src/hooks.server.js](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/src/hooks.server.js): Manage the user's session dynamically using cookies via `@supabase/ssr` so the server always knows who is logged in.
- **[MODIFY]** [src/routes/login/+page.svelte](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/src/routes/login/+page.svelte): Remove the manual password verification logic and connect the "Sign in" and "Google Login" buttons to the Supabase client.
- **[DELETE]** Custom username/password endpoints in `src/routes/api/auth/*` as Supabase Auth will govern registration and logins.

### Phase 3: Performance & SEO Optimization

- **[MODIFY]** [src/routes/+layout.svelte](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/src/routes/+layout.svelte) / [src/app.html](file:///home/alan/Documents/code/BMSC_ICT_CLUB_WEB/src/app.html): Inject standard `<meta>` tags (title, description, open graph tags) to ensure the site looks good when shared on social media and ranks appropriately on search engines.
- **[MODIFY]** Image Component Audits: Add `loading="lazy"` attributes to images below the fold to improve initial page load speed.
- **[MODIFY]** CSS Audits: Fine-tune any overly heavy animations or unoptimized responsive layouts that may cause lag on mobile devices.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run build` safely without any Prisma SQLite missing configuration errors.
- Ensure all SvelteKit endpoints build cleanly.

### Manual Verification
1. I will provide you with the exact console commands to run Prisma DB Push for the new PostgreSQL DB.
2. I will guide you on setting up Google Auth credentials in your Google Cloud Platform and pasting them into the Supabase Dashboard.
3. You will verify locally (`npm run dev`) that you can register a new user using the new Supabase-backed login page, and that your database populates within the Supabase Dashboard.
4. You will inspect the webpage's head tags using Developer Tools to visualize the SEO enhancements and test them on mobile views to ensure UI stability.
